outram-park-fork-pflotran
Part of Outram Park (outram-park-backend).

This crate is an independent fork / Rust translation of PFLOTRAN
  https://www.pflotran.org   (code: https://bitbucket.org/pflotran/pflotran)
PFLOTRAN is a massively-parallel subsurface flow and reactive-transport
simulator (Fortran + PETSc) developed cooperatively by the US Department of
Energy national laboratories — Los Alamos (LANL), Pacific Northwest (PNNL),
Oak Ridge (ORNL), Lawrence Berkeley (LBNL), and Sandia (SNL). Original authors
include Peter C. Lichtner, Glenn E. Hammond, Chuan Lu, Richard T. Mills,
Satish Karra, and the wider PFLOTRAN development team.

